scsi: ufs: qcom: SM6375 has no UFS PHY retention

With the default system suspend level (device sleep, link in hibern8) the
UFS PHY has to keep its state through the suspend. On SM6375 it does not
once the SoC reaches VDD min: every s2idle that reached it ended in
"ufshcd_uic_hibern8_exit: hibern8 exit failed. ret = 5" on resume and a
host reset (sunstone, SM4375; seven of seven, none in suspends that stayed
out of VDD min). With spm_lvl 5 (device power down, link off) the same
s2idle reaches VDD min and resumes cleanly.

Use the no_phy_retention drvdata, as for SM8550, which selects
UFS_PM_LVL_5 for system suspend.

Signed-off-by: 14sea <14sea@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
index 42eb6efd4..935a2c767 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -3009,12 +3009,17 @@ static const struct ufs_qcom_drvdata ufs_qcom_sm8550_drvdata = {
 	.no_phy_retention = true,
 };
 
+static const struct ufs_qcom_drvdata ufs_qcom_sm6375_drvdata = {
+	.no_phy_retention = true,
+};
+
 static const struct ufs_qcom_drvdata ufs_qcom_sa8255p_drvdata = {
 	.vops = &ufs_hba_qcom_sa8255p_vops
 };
 
 static const struct of_device_id ufs_qcom_of_match[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,ufshc" },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6375-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_sm6375_drvdata },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8550-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_sm8550_drvdata },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8650-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_sm8550_drvdata },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sa8255p-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_sa8255p_drvdata },
